part soc_7
  tally 2
  law
  note "SOC-7 · The survivor pension. v1 (months 2018-01 – 2025-06): a spouse aged 50 or over at the death is entitled to 85 % of the pension the deceased was entitled to on the day of the death, rounded, indexed as if it had started when the deceased's started (.1); paid from the month after the death if claimed within 12 months, otherwise from the month after the claim; the deceased's pension for the month of the death is due in full (.2); of two pensions one is paid, the elected one (.3)."
  note "v2 (months from 2025-07, published 2024-12-12): .1 and .2 as v1; the elected pension in full and a part of the other, 15 % for months July 2025 – December 2026 and 25 % from January 2027, rounded, both together never more than 3 times the MIN-PENSION in force for the month, the part cut to fit (.3); on a claim, one filed by 30 September 2025 effective from July 2025, a later one from the month after it; months before the decision paid as arrears with the first payment after it (.4)."

source soc_7 "Social Insurance Act, SOC-7 The survivor pension (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input soc7_cap_mult: int question "How many times MIN-PENSION may both pensions together come to (SOC-7 v2 .3)?"

input soc7_claim_by: date question "By what day must the claim be filed to take effect from the start of v2 (SOC-7 v2 .4)?"

input soc7_claim_months: int question "Within how many months of the death must the claim be filed to be paid from the month after the death (SOC-7 .2)?"

input soc7_death_month_full: bool question "Is the deceased's pension for the month of the death due in full (SOC-7 .2)?"

input soc7_min_age: int question "From what age at the death is the spouse entitled (SOC-7 .1)?"

input soc7_part: num question "What part of the second pension is paid for this month (SOC-7 v2 .3)?"

input soc7_rate: num question "What share of the deceased's pension is the survivor pension (SOC-7 .1)?"

input soc7_v2_from: date question "From what day does a timely claim take effect (SOC-7 v2 .4)?"

